{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>My soul thirsts</b> — Water satisfies a person for a moment and he lives, and his soul returns to him; but bread is not so. Therefore he compared his longing for the House of Elohim to the thirst of one thirsty for water. And because the life of humankind depends on water, therefore [the verse says] 'to El the living one.'" "<b>When shall I come</b> — He longs for the coming of the redeemer." "<b>That I may see the face of Elohim</b> — This is 'every male of yours shall be seen.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:32.929545124Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}